course: dictionary
lesson: 15250
title: Shipbuilders and the towns they built
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shipbuilder is a person whose job is designing or building ships. The word has two parts: ship and builder. A builder makes things, so a shipbuilder makes ships.
explain: «The shipbuilder drew the plans for the new ferry on a big sheet of paper.» Drawing plans is part of the job, so the shipbuilder is the person who designs the ship, not just the one who builds it.
explain: The word can also mean a company that builds ships. «The shipbuilder won an order for three new ferries.» A company cannot draw a plan, but it can win an order, so here the word means the company. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A shipbuilder is a person whose job is designing or building ships.
fact: A shipbuilder can also be a company that builds ships.
fact: A shipyard is the place where ships are built, and a dock is where ships are loaded, repaired or kept.
fact: Port towns such as Belfast, Glasgow on the Clyde and Newcastle grew rich from shipbuilding.
fact: Shipbuilding is the work of building ships, and when shipyards closed, many shipbuilders lost their jobs.
exercise: «The shipbuilder drew the plans for the new ferry on a big sheet of paper.» Who is the shipbuilder in this sentence? | A ship that carries passengers across the sea | A man who sells paper | *A person who designs and builds ships | A sailor who steers the ferry
exercise: Which word means the place where ships are built? | Cargo | Lighthouse | *Shipyard | Harbour
exercise: «Glasgow's shipbuilders were famous across the world.» What do shipbuilders most likely mean here? | Fish sellers at the market | Teachers who taught sailing | Tourists who visited the ships | *People or companies that built ships
test: «Hundreds of workers were employed at the shipyard, where the shipbuilders built huge liners from steel.» What did the shipbuilders build? | Bridges | Houses | Trains | *Huge ships
test: Which school subject teaches about hulls, floating and steel? | Music | *Technology | Swimming | Dance
exam: «The shipbuilders in the port town worked hard all year.» What is a shipbuilder? | A sailor who steers a ship | *A person whose job is designing or building ships | A ship that carries cargo across the sea | A dock where ships are repaired
